// Copyright (c) 2026 Roshan. All rights reserved.// Proprietary license — see LICENSE file for details.package com.roshan.persona.selfmodify/** * NOUS — Rhino sandbox execution result (Module 15 — Self-modify). * * Sealed hierarchy representing the outcome of a single Rhino sandbox * execution. Internal to [RhinoJsSandbox] — converted to a * `com.roshan.persona.common.Result<String>` at the public boundary so the * rest of NOUS doesn't need to know about Rhino-specific failure modes. * * Five variants — one success, four typed failures: * *  - [Success] — script returned a value, converted to String via Rhino's *    `Context.toString()`. Carries the wall-clock execution time so callers *    can log slow skills. * *  - [Timeout] — script exceeded the [SandboxLimits.maxExecutionMs] budget. *    The Rhino context is forcibly closed; partial state is discarded. * *  - [MemoryLimit] — script exceeded the [SandboxLimits.maxMemoryMb] budget. *    Rhino doesn't expose per-context memory accounting, so this is a *    JVM-heap check (coarse). Carries the heap usage at the point of abort. * *  - [SecurityViolation] — script attempted to access a blocked class or *    package (via the [SecurityClassShutter]). Carries the reason (which *    class/package was blocked). * *  - [ScriptError] — script threw a JS-level exception (e.g., `TypeError`, *    `ReferenceError`, `SyntaxError`). Carries the error message and the *    1-based source line number (from Rhino's `RhinoException.lineSource`). * * Why a separate sealed type (instead of returning `Result<String>` directly)? * * 1. The Rhino sandbox has *five* distinct failure modes that map awkwardly *    onto `AppError`'s three skill errors (NotFound, Crashed, TimedOut). *    Timeout → AppError.Skill.TimedOut is clear, but SecurityViolation and *    MemoryLimit are both "skill crashed" — losing useful diagnostic info. * * 2. The internal [SelfModifyEngine] needs to react differently to each *    failure: a Timeout might warrant a retry with a bigger budget; a *    SecurityViolation should permanently quarantine the skill; a *    ScriptError should be reported back to the LLM for self-correction. * * 3. The public boundary ([RhinoJsSandbox.execute]) converts to *    `Result<String>` so the rest of NOUS doesn't need to know about these *    distinctions — but the engine layer can pattern-match on the sealed *    type before conversion. * * @see RhinoJsSandbox * @see SelfModifyEngine */sealed class SandboxResult {    /**     * Script executed successfully and returned a value.     *     * @param output the script's return value, coerced to String via     *   `org.mozilla.javascript.Context.toString()`. `undefined` → "undefined",     *   `null` → "null", numbers/booleans → their JS `toString()` form,     *   objects → their `toString()` (or `[object Object]` if not overridden).     * @param durationMs wall-clock execution time, in milliseconds.     */    data class Success(        val output: String,        val durationMs: Long,    ) : SandboxResult()    /**     * Script exceeded the wall-clock execution budget.     *     * Rhino's instruction-count observer fired after [durationMs] of wall-clock     * time, exceeding the configured [SandboxLimits.maxExecutionMs]. The     * context was forcibly closed; partial state is discarded.     *     * Retryable: the caller may re-run with a larger budget if appropriate.     *     * @param durationMs actual execution time at the point of abort.     */    data class Timeout(        val durationMs: Long,    ) : SandboxResult()    /**     * Script exceeded the JVM heap budget.     *     * Rhino's instruction-count observer sampled the JVM heap usage and found     * it exceeded [SandboxLimits.maxMemoryMb]. The context was forcibly closed.     *     * Note: this is a coarse JVM-heap check, not a per-context allocation     * limit. A script that allocates and immediately frees large objects     * may evade detection until GC catches up. For tighter control, callers     * should use [SandboxLimits.STRICT].     *     * @param usedMb JVM heap usage at the point of abort, in megabytes.     */    data class MemoryLimit(        val usedMb: Int,    ) : SandboxResult()    /**     * Script attempted to access a blocked Java class or package.     *     * The [SecurityClassShutter] intercepted the access attempt and returned     * `false`, which Rhino translates into a `SecurityException`-like     * `EcmaError`. This is the strongest failure mode — it indicates the     * script is trying to escape the sandbox.     *     * NOT retryable: the script should be permanently quarantined.     *     * @param reason human-readable description of what was blocked (e.g.,     *   "Blocked class: java.io.FileInputStream").     */    data class SecurityViolation(        val reason: String,    ) : SandboxResult()    /**     * Script threw a JavaScript-level exception.     *     * The script itself threw (e.g., `throw new TypeError("x is undefined")`,     * `JSON.parse("{bad json}")`, `null.foo`). The exception's message and     * source line number are captured for diagnostic logging.     *     * Retryable only after the script is fixed (e.g., by an LLM self-correction     * loop in [SelfModifyEngine]).     *     * @param message the JS exception's `message` property (or its     *   `toString()` if no `message`).     * @param line 1-based source line number where the exception was thrown     *   (from `RhinoException.lineSource`/`lineNumber`). -1 if unavailable.     */    data class ScriptError(        val message: String,        val line: Int,    ) : SandboxResult()    /**     * Convert this result to a human-readable summary for logging.     *     * Used by [SelfModifyEngine] when emitting brain-trace events. The format     * is stable enough for log grepping but not for UI (use the typed fields     * directly for UI strings).     */    fun describe(): String = when (this) {        is Success -> "Success(output=${output.take(50).replace("\n", "\\n")}..., durationMs=$durationMs)"        is Timeout -> "Timeout(durationMs=$durationMs)"        is MemoryLimit -> "MemoryLimit(usedMb=$usedMb)"        is SecurityViolation -> "SecurityViolation(reason=$reason)"        is ScriptError -> "ScriptError(message=${message.take(100)}, line=$line)"    }}